zasm
------------------------------------------
zasm accepts source code using 8080 and Z80 syntax and can convert 8080 syntax
to Z80. It can generate binary files, Intel Hex or Motorola S19 files, and
specialized files for Sinclair and Jupiter Ace and .tzx tape files.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  zlib0-1.4-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  make-4.4.1-2
  zlib-devel-1.4-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/Megatokio/zasm

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/Megatokio/zasm.git

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack zasm-4.5.0-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./zasm-4.5.0-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/zasm-4.5.0-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/zasm-4.5.0-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(zasm)
  /usr/bin/zasm.exe
  /usr/share/doc/Cygwin/zasm.README
  /usr/share/doc/zasm/LICENSE
  /usr/share/doc/zasm/README.md

